module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.Grp.Adjunctions
public import Mathlib.Topology.Category.TopCat.Limits.Basic
import StacksCheckRecall

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u v vJ uJ vC uC

variable (alpha : Type u) {beta : Type v} [Group beta]
variable {J : Type uJ} [Category.{vJ} J]
variable {C : Type uC} [Category.{vC} C]
variable (F : J ⥤ C) [HasColimit F] (Y : C)

/- The source needs both the categorical free-object examples and the concrete compatible-family
formula for colimits. Verified candidates are `GrpCat.adj`, `AddCommGrpCat.adj`,
`FreeGroup.lift`, `FreeGroup.closure_range_of`, `colimit.homIso'`,
`IsColimit.corepresentableBy`, `IsColimit.ofCorepresentableBy`, and the `TopCat` limit/colimit
instances. The adjunctions are the standard reusable owners, while `FreeGroup.lift` and
`FreeGroup.closure_range_of` retain the source's concrete no-relations and generation clauses.
For the topological example, `colimit.homIso'` is preferable to the abstract corepresentability
pair because its compatible families literally match the displayed functor. It is more general
than the topological specialization in the source, so it is recorded as the canonical bridge;
`TopCat.topCat_hasColimits` remains the source-facing conclusion. The cardinal bounds used to
verify the preceding criterion are proof-method ingredients with no matching single mathlib
owner; the recalls expose the resulting universal properties without creating parallel local
cardinality APIs. -/

/- Remark 4.25.2 (1): the free group functor is left adjoint to the forgetful functor, which
packages the natural equivalence between maps `E → G` and group morphisms from the free group on
`E` to `G`. -/
@[stacks 0AHP "free group as left adjoint to the forgetful functor"]
#check (GrpCat.adj : GrpCat.free ⊣ forget GrpCat.{u})

/- Remark 4.25.2 (2): every map from the generators `E` to a group extends uniquely to a group
homomorphism from `FreeGroup E`; this is the concrete no-relations universal property. -/
@[stacks 0AHP "unique extension from free group generators"]
#check (FreeGroup.lift : (alpha → beta) ≃ (FreeGroup alpha →* beta))

/- Remark 4.25.2 (3): the canonical image of `E` generates `FreeGroup E`. -/
@[stacks 0AHP "free group generated by its canonical generators"]
#check (FreeGroup.closure_range_of alpha :
  Subgroup.closure (Set.range (FreeGroup.of : alpha → FreeGroup alpha)) = ⊤)

/- Remark 4.25.2 (4): the analogous free abelian group construction is the left adjoint
`AddCommGrpCat.free ⊣ forget AddCommGrpCat`. -/
@[stacks 0AHP "free abelian group as a free-forgetful adjunction"]
#check (AddCommGrpCat.adj : AddCommGrpCat.free ⊣ forget AddCommGrpCat.{u})

/- Remark 4.25.2 (5): the category of topological spaces has all small limits. -/
@[stacks 0AHP "topological spaces have all small limits"]
#check (TopCat.topCat_hasLimits : HasLimits TopCat.{u})

/- Remark 4.25.2 (6): canonically, morphisms from a colimit to `Y` are naturally equivalent to
compatible families of morphisms from the diagram objects to `Y`; specializing this API to
`TopCat` identifies a colimit with a representing object for the displayed functor. -/
@[stacks 0AHP "colimit corepresents compatible families of morphisms"]
#check (colimit.homIso' F Y :
  ULift.{uJ} (colimit F ⟶ Y : Type vC) ≅
    { p : ∀ j, F.obj j ⟶ Y //
      ∀ {j j'} (f : j ⟶ j'), F.map f ≫ p j' = p j })

/- Remark 4.25.2 (7): every small diagram of topological spaces has a colimit. -/
@[stacks 0AHP "topological spaces have all small colimits"]
#check (TopCat.topCat_hasColimits : HasColimits TopCat.{u})
